{#-
  Document skeleton: the Horizon Europe DMP sections mapped onto the Norwegian
  knowledge model (research.data.no:norway-generic).

  Section titles and numbering follow the EC "Template Horizon Europe Data
  Management Plan". Each block lists anchor questions as "<chapterKey>.<questionKey>"
  json.key pairs; keys are chapter-qualified because json.key is only unique within
  a chapter. Every anchor is a top-level question of a live (annotated) chapter, so
  its reply path is deterministic; follow-up questions and list items below an
  anchor are rendered recursively and must not be listed here.

  Anchors are rendered at most once per document (see renderByKey in
  _renderers.html.j2), so the first section listing a key wins.

  Selection is driven by the KM's "Horizon Europe" tag. Anchors that do not carry
  that tag but that the EC template explicitly asks for are marked [untagged] below;
  tools/check_sections.py reports both directions of that comparison.

  Questions used for the front matter (contributors, project metadata, DMP title,
  related DMPs) are handled in frontpage.html.j2 / contributors.html.j2 /
  projects.html.j2 and are absent here.

  A few tagged questions are deliberately left out because reviewers found them
  redundant in this document; they are listed as OMITTED in tools/check_sections.py
  with the reason, so the deviation stays visible rather than looking like an
  oversight. Section 5 in particular now reads guidelines first, then where the data
  actually live, with the IT security question last as the summary of what is at
  stake. Three untagged questions were dropped from it as not being about data
  security: "Will storage need change over time?", "Do you need a shared space with
  your collaborators to work on data analysis?" and "Does your computational
  approach require validation of results?".

  The list below is a single Jinja expression, so it takes no {# #} comments; notes
  about individual blocks belong here.
-#}
{#-
  Follow-up questions dropped wherever they occur below an anchor, by json.key.
  Anchors are chapter-qualified but follow-ups are reached by recursion, which does
  not carry the chapter along, so these keys are matched unqualified;
  tools/check_sections.py fails if one of them is not unique in the knowledge model.
-#}
{%- set omitFollowups = [
  "storageSolutionAssociated",
  "storageSolutionStructured",
  "descriptionStorageSolution"
] -%}
{%- set sections = [
  {
    "id": "sec-data-summary",
    "title": "1. Data Summary",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "anchors": [
          "reusingCollectingChapter.hasMeasuredData",
          "reusingCollectingChapter.hasNonMeasuredData",
          "reusingCollectingChapter.collectsPhysicalSample",
          "reusingCollectingChapter.reDatasetsRecords",
          "reusingCollectingChapter.gather",
          "storingProtectingChapter.expectedTotalVolume"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sec-fair-data",
    "title": "2. FAIR Data",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "heading": "2.1. Making data findable, including provisions for metadata",
        "anchors": [
          "creatingData.miaStandardsExist",
          "creatingData.connectRespectiveMetadata",
          "archivingPublishingChapter.identifyArchiveDepositing",
          "archivingPublishingChapter.distributions"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "2.2. Making data accessible",
        "anchors": [
          "archivingPublishingChapter.allOpenOverTime",
          "creatingData.dataUseRestrictions"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "2.3. Making data interoperable",
        "anchors": [
          "creatingData.usesVocabularies",
          "processingDataChapter.integratingDataSourcesMoreInfo",
          "processingDataChapter.integratingDataSourcesMoreSamples",
          "processingDataChapter.otherFormThanArchive"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "2.4. Increase data re-use",
        "anchors": [
          "reusingCollectingChapter.whoInterested",
          "creatingData.assignsLicense",
          "creatingData.collectedDataRights"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sec-other-outputs",
    "title": "3. Other research outputs",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "anchors": [
          "reusingCollectingChapter.generateResearchSoftware",
          "archivingPublishingChapter.softwarePackages"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sec-resource-allocation",
    "title": "4. Allocation of resources",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "anchors": [
          "responsibilitiesResourcesChapter.haveManagementResponsibilities",
          "responsibilitiesResourcesChapter.requiresSpecialist",
          "responsibilitiesResourcesChapter.requiresSpecialHardwareSoftware",
          "responsibilitiesResourcesChapter.specialArrangementsAccess",
          "processingDataChapter.planComputeCapacity",
          "responsibilitiesResourcesChapter.storageActivePhase",
          "responsibilitiesResourcesChapter.preservationArchivingAssociated",
